## 5. 3D scenes

Two scenes in total, never more than one WebGL canvas mounted at a time. All geometry is generated in code.

### 5.1 Hero object — "faceted form"
- An icosahedron (detail 4) whose vertices are displaced by 3D simplex noise in a custom vertex shader, so it slowly "breathes" between shapes. Flat-shaded facets (compute normals per face with `dFdx`/`dFdy` in the fragment shader) so the surface shows discrete facet tones — **no smooth gradient shading, no fog, no bloom, no environment map**.
- Material colour = `--accent`; one directional light + one low ambient light. Optionally overlay the same geometry as a thin wireframe in `--text` at 15% opacity.
- Motion: slow rotation (~0.05 rad/s), pointer parallax tilt (max 8°, damped), noise amplitude eases down as the user scrolls past the hero.
- Size: about 420px on desktop, 260px on mobile.

### 5.2 Research scene — "attention grid"
- A 14×14 `InstancedMesh` of small cubes on a plane, viewed at an isometric angle. Heights animate like a moving heat-map (a nod to Grad-CAM attention maps). Cubes use `--accent`; the base plane uses `--border`. Only animates while in view.

### 5.3 Performance rules for 3D (mandatory)
- **Poster first**: render a static inline SVG of the faceted form immediately (part of the HTML, no JS). The canvas loads later and cross-fades over it. The poster is what shows for low-end devices, reduced motion, no WebGL, and while loading.
- Load the 3D bundle with `next/dynamic` (`ssr: false`), only after `requestIdleCallback` (fallback `setTimeout` 1500ms) **and** only when the scene's container is within 200px of the viewport.
- Skip the canvas entirely (keep the poster) if any of: `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, `navigator.connection.saveData`, `navigator.deviceMemory <= 4`, `navigator.hardwareConcurrency <= 4`, WebGL unavailable, or a quick first-frames FPS probe averages under 30 fps (then unmount and show the poster).
- Canvas settings: `dpr={[1, 1.5]}`, `antialias` only when DPR is 1, `powerPreference: "low-power"`, `frameloop="demand"` with an invalidate loop that stops when the canvas is off-screen (IntersectionObserver) or the tab is hidden (`visibilitychange`).
- Dispose geometries/materials on unmount. Canvas is `aria-hidden="true"` and not focusable.

